## The frame again {#c8 number=8 target=80 summary="P followed back through every stage, and three takeaways." sources="process-ssr, copy-last-frame"}

### P, from the pre-pass to the floor {#c8-walk kind=2d graph=frame focus="PRE, SSR, OPAQUE, HISTORY"}

${cue "key" {' {callout "process-ssr"}}} Here is the path of P, the floor pixel in front of the teapot, through the frame once more.

P's depth and normal came from the depth pre-pass.

Its ray was marched through the depth pyramid.

${cue "key" {' {callout "copy-last-frame"}}} Its colour came from last frame's image.

Its blur came from the floor's roughness.

How much of that colour the floor shows came from P's validity.

### Three takeaways {#c8-takeaways kind=3d}

${cue "key" {opening demoRoom panelHidden {append baseRoom lowCamera}}}
${cue "key" {' {motion {' {cameraPath {' {' 18.0 10.0 5.6} {' 30.0 12.0 5.0} {' 22.0 10.0 5.4}}}}}}}

${overText {' {floorRoughnessRange 0.15 0.05}} "SSR knows only depths, normals"} ${cue "key" {' {motion {' {path {' cameraYaw} {' {' 24.0}} sentence}}}}}and last frame's colour.

${cue "key" {' {motion {' {path {' cameraYaw} {' {' 20.0}} sentence}}}}}So it can reflect only what was on screen.

${cue "key" {' {motion {' {path {' cameraDistance} {' {' 5.0}} sentence}}}}}It traces one ray per half-size pixel, through a pyramid of depths.

${overText {' {floorRoughnessRange 0.05 0.03}} "It reuses last frame's light, so reflections of reflections build up, one bounce a frame"}.

${overText {' {floorRoughnessRange 0.03 0.3}} "And it blurs by roughness with a chain of mip levels, not with a blur per pixel"}.

${cue "key" {' {motion {' {path {' cameraDistance} {' {' 5.6}} sentence}}}}}${overText {' {ssrEnabledRange 1.0 0.0}} "What is off screen is lost, and what has moved lags a frame"}.

${over {' {ssrEnabledRange 0.0 1.0}} {overText {' {floorRoughnessRange 0.3 0.04}} "And the fades keep every pixel's validity at fifty-eight hundredths or less, so SSR only ever covers part of the sky's reflection"}}.

### Where to read {#c8-sources kind=2d sources="process-ssr, copy-last-frame"}

These are the lines of Godot's source that this chapter returned to.

They are the passes, and the copy of last frame's image that closes the loop.
